# Security-sensitive paths, listed on their own so that adding a co-maintainer to the
# line above doesn't also hand them these by accident. The last matching pattern wins,
# so these lines must stay below `*`. Give someone one of these paths only on purpose.
#
# - .github/: the workflows, their lockfile and scripts, Dependabot, the issue forms and this file
# - Dockerfile and .grype.yaml: the container image and its vulnerability gate (ADR-0011)
# - deny.toml: the advisory, ban, licence and source policy for dependencies
# - packaging/: install scripts, the npm launcher and the tap and bucket workflows (ADR-0010)
# - xtask/ and .cargo/: the release logic (builds, archives, checksums, channel files and
#   release notes) and the `cargo xtask` alias that CI and the release workflow call (ADR-0009)
# - crates/agent-grimoire-install/: the code that writes to a user's project (ADR-0006)
# - crates/agent-grimoire-resolve/: version resolution and permission consent
# - crates/agent-grimoire-adapters/: what each client is given, such as an agent's tool list,
#   an MCP server's command and environment, and hooks
# - crates/agent-grimoire-mcp/: MCP server transport, limit and authorization defaults (ADR-0007)
# - catalog/skills/, catalog/tools/ and catalog/mcp-servers/: code that runs on users'
#   machines (a skill can bundle scripts)
# - plugins/ and .claude-plugin/: the Claude Code marketplace, which users add from this
#   repository, not from a release
